'''Al Alcor''' was a location in [[the galaxy]].<ref name="PastTheBarrier" /> Around [[9 ABY]],<ref name="SkelCrewDate">{{SkeletonCrewDate}}</ref> after a [[Skeleton Crew|group]] of [[Youngling|children]] found the [[starship]]<ref name="Real Adventure">{{SkeletonCrew|This Could Be a Real Adventure}}</ref> ''[[Onyx Cinder]]''<ref name="Onyx Cinder">{{Databank|onyx-cinder|Onyx Cinder}}</ref> on the [[planet]] [[At Attin]], the [[human]] [[Gender|boy]] [[Wim]] accidentally caused it to jump to [[hyperspace]].<ref name="Real Adventure" /> The children then met the [[droid]] [[SM-33]] aboard the ship, and the human girl [[Fern]] told him to take her and her companions back to At Attin. As the droid was unable to recall At Attin, he suggested other locations she could have meant, including Al Alcor and<ref name="PastTheBarrier" /> the [[planet]]s<ref name="Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia: The Comprehensive Guide to the Star Wars Galaxy]]''</ref> [[Atollon]] and [[Aldhani]].<ref name="PastTheBarrier" />

==Behind the scenes==
Al Alcor was mentioned in "[[Way, Way Out Past the Barrier]],"<ref name="PastTheBarrier" /> the second episode of the [[Disney+]] series ''[[Star Wars: Skeleton Crew]]'',<ref name="Guide">{{SW|url=series/skeleton-crew/season-1-episode-2-episode-guide|text="Way, Way Out Past the Barrier" Episode Guide &#124; Star Wars: Skeleton Crew}}</ref> which aired on [[December 2]], [[2024]].<ref name="Early">{{SW|url=news/skeleton-crew-premiere-date|text=''Star Wars: Skeleton Crew'' Will Debut Early|date=2024-11-26}}</ref>

